	(text "Clock Distribution -- shared 38.4MHz reference"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.74 24.892 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "33333333-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "THE defining block of this board's architecture. All four DW3210 receivers\nrun from ONE reference, which is what makes TDoA across them possible at\nall: 1ns of clock error is 30cm of position error, and at this board's 1m\nbaseline 1cm of differential path error is 10cm of position error at 10m.\n\nA passive crystal CANNOT be shared. Each DW3000's XTI/XTO pair forms its\nown oscillator, so four chips sharing one crystal would be four oscillators\n-- the problem, not the fix. The topology is:\n\n  38.4MHz TCXO -> 1:4 low-skew fan-out buffer -> 2200pF AC coupling\n  -> each DW3210 XTI (pin 21), with 1pF from each XTO (pin 22) to GND.\n\nTCXO/buffer parts are NOT yet selected (open item, docs/decisions.md).\nRequired spec, from the real Qorvo DW3000 Datasheet v1.3 Table 10,\n'External Reference (For example a TCXO)':\n  Amplitude     0.8V to VDD2, Vpp\n  Coupling      MUST be AC coupled; 2200pF recommended\n  Phase noise   -132 dBc/Hz @1kHz, -145 dBc/Hz @10kHz\n  Duty cycle    40-60%\nXTO note is from the same datasheet's pin table: 'Requires 1pF to the\nground, only if external clock is used, otherwise leave empty.'\n\nBuffer output-to-output skew is a FIXED per-chip offset and calibrates out\nalongside cable delay -- only skew STABILITY matters, which on-board is\nnegligible. Keep the four buffer-to-XTI traces length-matched anyway.\n\nPlaced here are only the passives whose values the datasheet actually\nspecifies. TCXO and buffer symbols get added when the parts are chosen."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.962 54.864 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "33333333-0000-4000-8000-000000000002")
